WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.060
A fruit fly cell holds eight chromosomes.

2
00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.360
Its eggs and sperm hold four.

3
00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:16.380
Which four? Mendel worked out his laws from counts of peas.

4
00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.260
He never saw what did the separating.

5
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:23.620
A cell division called meiosis does it.

6
00:00:24.383 --> 00:00:27.203
Follow one pair of homologous chromosomes.

7
00:00:28.323 --> 00:00:31.883
Homologs are the two members of a pair, one from each parent.

8
00:00:33.083 --> 00:00:39.803
This fly carries two alleles of one gene: capital A on one homolog, small a on the

9
00:00:39.803 --> 00:00:45.723
other. In S phase, each chromosome is copied into two sister chromatids.

10
00:00:46.683 --> 00:00:48.383
Count centromeres, not arms.

11
00:00:48.943 --> 00:00:50.263
It is still one chromosome.

12
00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:56.663
Meiosis is one round of DNA replication followed by two divisions.

13
00:00:57.523 --> 00:01:02.123
In prophase I, homologs pair along their length, as a bivalent.

14
00:01:03.083 --> 00:01:06.803
At metaphase I, the two homologs face opposite poles.

15
00:01:07.943 --> 00:01:13.323
Anaphase I pulls them apart, so capital A and small a go to different cells.

16
00:01:14.217 --> 00:01:16.157
Count the centromeres again.

17
00:01:17.057 --> 00:01:22.217
Each cell has one chromosome of this pair, so each is already haploid.

18
00:01:22.957 --> 00:01:28.837
The chromosome still has two sister chromatids, and no copying comes before meiosis

19
00:01:28.837 --> 00:01:34.277
II. Meiosis II pulls the sisters apart, as a mitosis would.

20
00:01:35.137 --> 00:01:39.957
Two of the four products carry capital A, and two carry small a.

21
00:01:40.617 --> 00:01:44.657
That is the law of segregation, seen as chromosome movement.

22
00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:51.810
Now add a second gene, with alleles capital B and small b, on a different

23
00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:58.890
chromosome. Each pair can face the spindle two ways, and how one pair faces does not

24
00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:00.170
affect how another does.

25
00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:08.990
In one meiosis, the four products are 2 capital A capital B and 2 small a small b.

26
00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:18.690
In another, they are 2 capital A small b and 2 small a capital B. Ignore crossing over.

28
00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:25.513
Across many meioses, the two orientations are equally likely, so each of the four

29
00:02:25.513 --> 00:02:27.273
kinds makes up one quarter.

30
00:02:28.653 --> 00:02:36.413
With four pairs, the fly has 2 times 2 times 2 times 2, or 16 chromosome

31
00:02:36.413 --> 00:02:38.733
combinations, ignoring crossing over.

32
00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:47.053
Pairs orient on their own at metaphase I. Remember the rule: meiosis I separates

33
00:02:47.053 --> 00:02:50.333
homologs, and meiosis II separates sisters.
